+Resolution is **install-time only** — dispatch stays zero-cost. After installing the main plugin, missing dependencies are resolved transitively (metadata-only, nothing downloaded during planning; a per-name record of the strictest `min_version` seen, plus a depth bound, make metadata cycles an error rather than a hang), listed apt-style, and installed after one confirmation (`--yes` skips, `--no-deps` opts out). A declined plan is a warning, not a failure. Dependencies already satisfied from raw `$PATH` or a local-dev install count as satisfied, with a warning when `min_version` can't be verified.
